WEBVTT

01:03.563 --> 01:05.732
SUNDAY, JUNE 1, 2025
I HELPED MOM MAKE LUNCH TODAY

01:18.787 --> 01:20.747
CHECK TODAY'S TO-DO LIST

01:22.749 --> 01:25.085
HAN SEO-YOON

01:25.168 --> 01:27.378
ALARM

01:44.646 --> 01:49.400
YOU HAVE MEMORY DISORDER FROM AN ACCIDENT
CHECK YOUR COMPUTER ON THE DESK!

01:49.484 --> 01:51.903
WHEN YOU WAKE UP,
YOUR MEMORY RESETS TO BEFORE THE ACCIDENT

01:51.986 --> 01:54.739
CHECK YOUR NOTES AND JOURNAL
WHEN YOU WAKE UP IN THE MORNING

01:54.823 --> 01:56.491
HAN SEO-YOON
HAESOL HIGH SCHOOL JUNIOR, CLASS 5, NO. 29

01:56.574 --> 01:58.451
ALWAYS KEEP THE NOTEBOOK IN YOUR BAG

01:58.535 --> 02:00.411
CHECK TODAY'S TO-DOS ON THE CALENDAR!

02:00.495 --> 02:03.289
CHECK YOUR JOURNAL ON THE COMPUTER!
ALWAYS WRITE DOWN THINGS TO REMEMBER!

02:15.677 --> 02:17.387
On January 8, 2025,

02:17.971 --> 02:20.932
you got in a car accident
that left you with a memory disorder.

02:22.559 --> 02:23.518
When you fall asleep,

02:24.060 --> 02:27.188
your memory resets the next morning
to the moment of the accident.

02:27.981 --> 02:28.857
It's a condition

02:29.357 --> 02:30.859
called anterograde amnesia.

02:34.112 --> 02:35.864
The only people who know about it

02:36.489 --> 02:39.909
are your parents, Ji-min,
and the teachers at school.

02:41.494 --> 02:44.455
You've been keeping a journal
every day since the accident.

03:04.851 --> 03:05.810
Did you sleep well?

03:06.394 --> 03:08.021
- Have some breakfast.
- Okay.

03:09.898 --> 03:12.066
- Did you do your homework?
- We had homework?

03:12.150 --> 03:14.277
- Why didn't you tell us before?
- So, none of you did it?

03:14.360 --> 03:15.653
Hey, the bus is here.

03:28.708 --> 03:30.251
Hi, Han Seo-yoon.

03:30.335 --> 03:32.962
Why draw attention?
You think she'll be friends with you?

03:33.504 --> 03:35.048
We're classmates, so we are friends.

03:35.131 --> 03:37.592
Do you hear yourself?

03:37.675 --> 03:39.302
Don't be an idiot.

03:39.385 --> 03:42.805
- You're so embarrassing.
- "So we are friends." What a joke.

03:44.682 --> 03:46.601
She's really pretty, isn't she?

03:49.395 --> 03:50.980
Hey, you have a girlfriend.

03:52.190 --> 03:53.483
I told you I liked her first.

03:54.150 --> 03:56.027
That's true.

03:56.110 --> 03:57.570
Do something, then.

03:57.654 --> 03:59.364
No, I can't.

04:00.740 --> 04:02.075
Why not? Just go for it.

04:02.158 --> 04:03.618
How can I?

04:31.271 --> 04:33.356
You punks! Are you trying to get killed?

04:34.274 --> 04:36.150
- What the hell?
- Jeez, man.

04:36.234 --> 04:38.444
- Are you okay?
- Sir, watch your driving!

04:38.528 --> 04:39.696
What the heck was that?

04:45.368 --> 04:46.327
That really hurt.

04:46.411 --> 04:48.162
I think it'll bruise.

04:55.378 --> 04:56.754
I'm sorry.

04:58.214 --> 04:59.340
I'm really sorry.

05:27.243 --> 05:28.995
I told you that's not how you do it.

05:29.078 --> 05:30.079
You idiot.

05:30.163 --> 05:32.123
- You need to hold it like this.
- What about you?

05:32.206 --> 05:34.709
All right. Let's just go.

06:02.862 --> 06:03.696
Hey.

06:05.448 --> 06:07.158
Why do you keep putting up with that?

06:08.785 --> 06:09.619
Sorry.

06:26.552 --> 06:29.097
You punks! Seriously.

06:29.180 --> 06:31.057
- Jeez.
- He had on his head some…

06:31.140 --> 06:33.726
- Hey. What's with him?
- What?

06:33.810 --> 06:35.686
You made a mess on my desk.

06:37.021 --> 06:38.731
Oh, you're Dong-sik's deskmate, right?

06:38.815 --> 06:40.691
I might have. Sorry.

06:40.775 --> 06:42.026
Do you find that stuff funny?

06:43.277 --> 06:44.570
Yeah, it makes me feel alive.

06:46.447 --> 06:47.281
Give it a rest.

06:48.199 --> 06:50.451
Stop bullying Dong-sik.
Don't you feel bad for him?

06:50.535 --> 06:52.787
What, are you his boyfriend?
Do you think they're dating?

06:52.870 --> 06:54.497
- What? For real?
- Oh, shit.

06:54.580 --> 06:57.208
- Han Seo-yoon's getting asked out again.
- It never ends, huh?

06:57.291 --> 06:58.960
- She's so stuck-up.
- She shot him down quick.

06:59.043 --> 07:00.628
- She is pretty though.
- Should I try next?

07:01.212 --> 07:03.131
- I did it once, and she shot me down.
- You idiot.

07:03.881 --> 07:06.384
- You're such a lunatic.
- Hey, you should ask Han Seo-yoon out.

07:07.969 --> 07:09.011
You want me to do what?

07:09.595 --> 07:10.680
Tell her you like her.

07:12.598 --> 07:16.018
- You want me to ask her out?
- Yeah.

07:16.853 --> 07:17.770
Why?

07:18.396 --> 07:19.230
No reason.

07:19.313 --> 07:21.065
Forget it.

07:21.149 --> 07:22.984
Why did I bother coming over? I'm off.

07:23.067 --> 07:25.778
Hey, Dung-sik. You ask her out, then!

07:25.862 --> 07:27.822
- Hey, get back here!
- Since when were you there?

07:27.905 --> 07:30.074
- Come here, dude!
- Dung-sik!

08:03.274 --> 08:04.317
What am I doing?

08:11.324 --> 08:15.286
HEY, TURN AROUND AND LOOK UP
AT THE CLASSROOM WINDOW

08:22.668 --> 08:23.753
JAE-WON ♥ SEO-YOON

08:36.474 --> 08:37.475
It's similar.

08:37.558 --> 08:38.643
Here's a modern translation.

08:39.685 --> 08:42.063
"Are you really leaving?"

08:42.146 --> 08:43.814
"Are you leaving me behind?"

08:44.815 --> 08:46.817
So, we went over "Gashiri" today.

08:46.901 --> 08:49.237
I'M SORRY FOR ALL THE TROUBLE

08:49.320 --> 08:51.364
Make sure to review the characteristics
I mentioned at the end,

08:51.447 --> 08:55.576
and look over the materials
for the next class if you can.

08:55.660 --> 08:58.913
All right, that's it for today.
Enjoy your lunch.

08:58.996 --> 09:00.748
- Yes, sir!
- Yes, sir!

09:00.831 --> 09:02.708
Let's hurry!

09:02.792 --> 09:04.502
- There'll be a line!
- Let's go!

09:05.086 --> 09:05.962
Kim Jae-won.

09:06.045 --> 09:07.755
Hey, Dung-sik!

09:09.215 --> 09:10.716
- You haven't left for lunch.
- What's up?

09:13.636 --> 09:16.097
So, have you made up your mind?

09:16.180 --> 09:17.390
Is that really all you want?

09:18.057 --> 09:19.642
I'll just ask her and leave it at that.

09:19.725 --> 09:21.102
Yeah, just do that.

09:21.185 --> 09:22.186
Keep your word.

09:24.230 --> 09:27.441
- Hey, he's actually going to do it!
- You're so cool, Jae-won!

09:31.571 --> 09:32.446
Hey.

09:38.202 --> 09:39.120
Will you go out with me?

09:43.708 --> 09:45.751
I think he's really doing it. Hurry!

09:47.878 --> 09:49.005
Hey, start filming. Hurry.

09:52.592 --> 09:53.551
He's doing it.

09:54.343 --> 09:56.012
Is he really doing it?

10:02.476 --> 10:03.352
Okay.

10:04.353 --> 10:05.313
Okay.

10:08.274 --> 10:09.984
Wait, what?

10:11.319 --> 10:12.320
I'd like that.

10:12.403 --> 10:13.404
Let's go out.

10:14.238 --> 10:16.240
- What did she say?
- I don't believe it.

10:16.324 --> 10:17.867
- Let's meet after school.
- For real?

10:17.950 --> 10:19.577
- I'll go first.
- What?

10:20.536 --> 10:22.204
Why would she say yes?

10:22.288 --> 10:23.623
- What? Why?
- What?

10:24.707 --> 10:25.875
What the heck?

10:26.792 --> 10:28.711
Why?

10:31.631 --> 10:33.924
- Hey. Stay still.
- What are you doing?

10:36.552 --> 10:38.888
For example, y is equal

10:38.971 --> 10:40.640
- to x squared plus three.
- Jae-won.

10:40.723 --> 10:45.478
It's shifted up by three units,
and y equals x minus two squared.

10:46.103 --> 10:47.313
- How does it shift?
- How manly.

10:48.439 --> 10:51.567
- He's so cool.
- It shifts two units to the right.

11:00.034 --> 11:02.953
Hurry up. I'm starving.

11:10.711 --> 11:11.712
Hi.

11:15.132 --> 11:16.300
Hi.

11:28.312 --> 11:30.189
You're Kim Jae-won, right?

11:30.272 --> 11:31.482
Yeah, that's right.

11:32.066 --> 11:33.109
Give me your phone.

11:37.321 --> 11:38.155
Why?

11:49.333 --> 11:50.167
Here.

11:52.670 --> 11:54.630
"Junior, Class 2, Kim Jae-won."

11:55.339 --> 11:58.092
"My boyfriend is a man of few words."

11:58.175 --> 11:59.635
Did you call me your boyfriend?

12:00.386 --> 12:01.220
Yeah.

12:02.388 --> 12:04.807
What? You asked me out first.

12:05.558 --> 12:06.642
Isn't that right,

12:06.725 --> 12:08.018
boyfriend?

12:08.102 --> 12:10.813
Oh, right. I did.

12:13.524 --> 12:15.901
You see, the thing is…

12:18.404 --> 12:20.948
Some kids are bullying my deskmate,

12:21.949 --> 12:24.118
so I couldn't just sit back and watch.

12:24.201 --> 12:25.995
They promised they'd stop bullying him

12:26.078 --> 12:28.164
if I asked you out.

12:29.206 --> 12:30.332
That's why I did it.

12:31.333 --> 12:32.376
I'm sorry.

12:34.628 --> 12:35.838
You're a good friend.

12:37.882 --> 12:39.258
We're just deskmates, really.

12:40.259 --> 12:42.386
Well, I don't care what the reason is.

12:42.470 --> 12:43.721
Does it matter to you?

12:43.804 --> 12:46.390
Do you not want to go out with me?

12:46.474 --> 12:48.476
- No, I--
- All right, then.

12:50.394 --> 12:53.147
It's not that I don't want to, but…

12:54.023 --> 12:55.274
Do you…

12:57.735 --> 12:58.569
like me?

12:58.652 --> 12:59.570
No.

12:59.653 --> 13:00.696
Then, why?

13:02.198 --> 13:04.033
I want to try something new.

13:06.076 --> 13:07.536
Otherwise, life gets boring.

13:07.620 --> 13:08.829
You're on board, right?

13:09.788 --> 13:12.416
But I have a few dating conditions.

13:13.417 --> 13:14.293
Number one,

13:14.376 --> 13:16.086
we keep communication short.

13:16.921 --> 13:17.755
Number two,

13:17.838 --> 13:19.840
we don't talk to each other
until after school.

13:20.424 --> 13:21.467
Number three,

13:21.550 --> 13:23.093
we don't catch real feelings.

13:24.929 --> 13:25.971
- What do you--
- Let's go.

13:26.055 --> 13:26.931
Go where?

13:31.101 --> 13:32.019
Am I supposed to come?

13:32.686 --> 13:33.604
Yeah!

13:35.356 --> 13:36.607
What's your favorite season?

13:36.690 --> 13:37.691
My favorite season?

13:38.317 --> 13:39.151
Summer.

13:39.735 --> 13:40.653
Favorite number?

13:43.405 --> 13:44.990
- Five.
- "Five."

13:45.574 --> 13:46.408
Favorite subject?

13:47.034 --> 13:49.495
I guess Korean history.

13:50.246 --> 13:51.956
- Korean history?
- Yeah.

13:54.333 --> 13:55.459
What's your favorite food?

13:55.543 --> 13:57.545
I like anything with meat.

13:57.628 --> 13:58.921
What are you doing, by the way?

13:59.755 --> 14:01.090
We're a couple starting today,

14:01.173 --> 14:03.384
so I should know you a little better.

14:05.553 --> 14:06.387
There we go.

14:13.894 --> 14:14.770
Hey.

14:17.064 --> 14:18.440
Black bean noodles
or spicy seafood noodle soup?

14:19.316 --> 14:20.192
Black bean noodles.

14:20.276 --> 14:21.235
"Black bean noodles."

14:22.736 --> 14:24.947
Do you like hard or soft peaches?

14:26.282 --> 14:28.909
I'm allergic to peaches.

14:30.536 --> 14:31.412
That's a shame.

14:32.746 --> 14:33.831
"Allergic."

14:34.874 --> 14:36.417
What's your MBTI?

14:37.001 --> 14:38.669
I've never taken the test.

14:40.170 --> 14:41.755
- Are you serious?
- I'm going to do it.

14:43.215 --> 14:44.675
- Do it soon.
- Okay.

14:45.384 --> 14:47.094
What's your favorite game?

14:48.053 --> 14:50.389
I'm not really into games.

14:50.472 --> 14:51.724
"Not into games."

14:51.807 --> 14:52.850
Favorite K-pop idol?

14:52.933 --> 14:54.393
I'm not really

14:55.561 --> 14:56.604
into them either.

14:57.229 --> 14:58.105
So, no favorites?

15:00.107 --> 15:01.191
I see.

15:03.986 --> 15:06.155
"MBTI,

15:07.031 --> 15:08.657
favorite game, and fanboy interests

15:09.366 --> 15:10.242
are unclear."

15:20.586 --> 15:21.670
Hello.

15:22.421 --> 15:23.255
Hello.

15:29.428 --> 15:30.346
Come on.

15:59.208 --> 16:00.542
Oh, I do have a favorite song.

16:01.669 --> 16:02.503
What is it?

16:03.629 --> 16:04.505
Hold on.

16:08.801 --> 16:09.635
Hang on.

16:11.470 --> 16:12.304
I like this one.

16:12.388 --> 16:14.014
"GOOD NIGHT GOOD DREAM"
NERD CONNECTION

16:14.098 --> 16:15.140
I should check it out.

16:15.224 --> 16:17.226
You really don't have to do that.

16:18.310 --> 16:20.145
What's your favorite sport?

16:20.229 --> 16:21.480
I don't like sports.

16:22.314 --> 16:23.357
What?

16:23.440 --> 16:24.316
Why not?

16:25.150 --> 16:27.152
You look like you'd be great at sports.

16:28.612 --> 16:29.446
It makes you sweaty.

16:30.280 --> 16:31.198
What?

16:32.866 --> 16:33.951
Why are you laughing?

16:37.079 --> 16:39.873
Are you a germaphobe or something?

16:40.916 --> 16:43.752
Come on. I'm not a germaphobe.

16:44.545 --> 16:47.214
I just care about cleanliness.

16:47.297 --> 16:50.300
- You care about…
- I care about cleanliness.

16:50.384 --> 16:52.052
"Cares about cleanliness."

16:52.136 --> 16:53.846
By the way,
why are you writing down all this?

16:55.055 --> 16:57.141
You don't seem like the ordinary type.

16:58.058 --> 16:58.976
No?

17:00.436 --> 17:01.687
I could say the same about you.

17:04.857 --> 17:07.568
I guess I'm not exactly ordinary.

17:41.018 --> 17:43.103
Why are you still up?

17:43.187 --> 17:45.147
Keep that up, and you won't grow taller.

17:45.230 --> 17:47.816
Like I need to.
I'm taller than you now, Dad.

17:47.900 --> 17:50.069
- What?
- Have dinner. I made soybean paste stew.

17:51.528 --> 17:52.905
Oh dear. I already ate.

17:52.988 --> 17:55.532
Just leave it.
I'll have it for breakfast tomorrow.

17:56.617 --> 17:58.577
Go to bed already.

18:17.971 --> 18:20.140
HAN SEO-YOON
GOOD NIGHT

18:23.936 --> 18:25.145
Number one,

18:25.229 --> 18:26.897
we keep communication short.

18:27.981 --> 18:29.566
She's so quirky.

18:32.152 --> 18:33.320
Wait up!

18:39.284 --> 18:40.494
- Hey!
- Hey.

18:49.711 --> 18:50.546
It's Kim Jae-won.

18:50.629 --> 18:52.089
- Hey!
- It's Kim Jae-won.

19:03.517 --> 19:04.643
Hi.

19:30.377 --> 19:31.628
Number two,

19:31.712 --> 19:33.755
we don't talk to each other
until after school.

19:56.320 --> 19:57.154
What?

19:57.738 --> 19:58.822
Stop.

19:58.906 --> 19:59.990
Stop what?

20:00.073 --> 20:02.951
I want you to stop dating Seo-yoon.

20:04.536 --> 20:05.370
Why?

20:05.454 --> 20:06.997
You don't even like her.

20:09.082 --> 20:10.417
How would you know that?

20:12.002 --> 20:14.338
You've never even
said hello to her before.

20:21.553 --> 20:22.471
I'm curious

20:23.680 --> 20:24.765
about what kind of person she is.

20:27.309 --> 20:28.310
Let me see your phone.

20:32.731 --> 20:34.650
Wait. Is she getting his number?

20:35.651 --> 20:37.194
Oh, we've got a love triangle.

20:37.277 --> 20:38.320
He's so cool.

20:39.821 --> 20:41.198
- He is.
- Give it back.

20:41.281 --> 20:42.658
- I don't think so.
- It's mine. Give it back.

20:42.741 --> 20:44.243
- Hey, Jin!
- Give it back.

20:44.326 --> 20:45.619
Oh jeez.

20:45.702 --> 20:47.204
Sorry.

20:47.287 --> 20:48.288
What is this?

20:48.372 --> 20:50.040
You crazy punk.

20:50.123 --> 20:51.250
- Hey, pass.
- Hey!

20:51.333 --> 20:53.043
- What is it?
- Stop it.

20:53.126 --> 20:54.419
Hey, pass it.

20:54.503 --> 20:55.671
It's mine. Give it back.

20:56.546 --> 20:58.423
- Pass it again.
- Hey, Gi-hyeon!

20:59.091 --> 21:00.092
You're such an otaku.

21:00.175 --> 21:02.928
- Give it back. It's mine.
- Why should I?

21:09.893 --> 21:10.769
Knock it off.

21:11.353 --> 21:12.479
He doesn't like it.

21:15.732 --> 21:16.566
You don't like it?

21:19.653 --> 21:20.612
We made a deal.

21:26.451 --> 21:27.869
- Hi, Kim Jae-won.
- Oh jeez.

21:30.747 --> 21:31.957
- What?
- You smell nice.

21:32.040 --> 21:33.667
You smell really nice.

21:34.167 --> 21:35.460
I do?

21:35.544 --> 21:36.378
Yeah.

21:38.714 --> 21:40.090
I think it's just the fabric softener.

21:40.173 --> 21:41.216
You're free, right?

21:41.300 --> 21:42.551
Right now?

21:42.634 --> 21:44.303
- Let's go.
- Go where?

21:51.727 --> 21:53.103
Oh, I got it!

21:55.439 --> 21:56.898
Get out of the way. I can't see!

21:57.524 --> 21:58.442
I can't lose.

21:58.525 --> 22:00.652
- You picked an easy one on purpose.
- No, I didn't.

22:05.657 --> 22:06.491
Can you handle this?

22:07.617 --> 22:08.452
No.

22:08.535 --> 22:10.162
BULDAK FIRE NOODLES

22:10.662 --> 22:11.705
I can't handle it!

22:20.672 --> 22:21.590
- Is it too spicy?
- No.

22:23.383 --> 22:24.634
I need something to drink.

22:24.718 --> 22:26.386
You can't finish it?

22:31.266 --> 22:32.476
I have a headache.

22:35.771 --> 22:37.481
…HE WENT TO GET A DRINK,
AND THAT WAS KIND OF CUTE

22:41.443 --> 22:42.652
Kim Jae-won!

22:47.449 --> 22:48.533
Jeez.

22:48.617 --> 22:49.659
Let's go.

22:51.078 --> 22:52.120
Let's go.

22:52.204 --> 22:53.080
Okay.

23:03.381 --> 23:04.341
No way.

23:06.259 --> 23:07.636
Let's bend down.

23:20.440 --> 23:21.483
Jeez, you scared me!

23:34.830 --> 23:36.123
Kim Jae-won!

23:39.751 --> 23:41.545
"GOOD NIGHT GOOD DREAM"

23:43.004 --> 23:46.424
What was it about me

23:46.508 --> 23:49.511
That you loved

23:50.220 --> 23:54.599
So deeply about me?

23:57.602 --> 24:04.359
All I can offer you now is

24:04.985 --> 24:09.948
Good night, good dream, goodbye

24:12.284 --> 24:18.498
Good night, good dream, goodbye

24:22.377 --> 24:26.131
I WANTED JAE-WON TO SING A FEW MORE SONGS,
BUT HE WAS TOO SHY

24:29.009 --> 24:31.553
- Hey, get him!
- Get him!

24:31.636 --> 24:33.221
- Hey!
- Get him!

24:33.305 --> 24:35.056
Hey, put that down!

24:38.393 --> 24:41.313
- Hey, get that punk!
- Come here, you bastard!

24:41.396 --> 24:43.481
- Hey!
- Get him!

24:43.565 --> 24:44.482
Hey!

24:44.566 --> 24:46.151
Let go!

24:46.234 --> 24:48.737
Let go, asshole!

24:48.820 --> 24:50.030
Let go!

24:54.576 --> 24:56.411
- You bastard.
- Come at me, asshole.

24:56.494 --> 24:57.621
- Get him.
- You crazy bastard.

24:57.704 --> 24:58.872
- You asshole.
- Come here.

25:01.416 --> 25:02.417
What the hell was that?

25:03.168 --> 25:05.253
- Forget him. Get him off him.
- Damn it.

25:05.879 --> 25:08.006
- You asshole!
- You bastard!

25:08.715 --> 25:10.050
- Damn it.
- Let go!

25:10.133 --> 25:11.134
Let go, you bastard!

25:14.346 --> 25:15.889
That goddamn psycho!

25:22.020 --> 25:23.897
- You son of a bitch!
- Come here!

25:23.980 --> 25:26.316
- You asshole!
- You bastard!

25:26.399 --> 25:27.609
Stomp him!

25:27.692 --> 25:30.237
Stomp him!

25:32.113 --> 25:33.448
You piece of shit.

25:34.241 --> 25:36.785
- What's this?
- Who the hell was that?

25:36.868 --> 25:39.079
Is that asshole out of his mind?

25:42.415 --> 25:43.750
- Get over here.
- Come here.

25:44.584 --> 25:45.502
You son of a bitch.

25:47.087 --> 25:48.129
You're getting me too!

25:49.130 --> 25:51.132
Stop that, you piece of shit!

25:51.216 --> 25:52.592
I said stop it!

25:52.676 --> 25:54.052
Stop it!

25:56.471 --> 26:00.725
- I'm going to kill you too!
- Teacher! Help!

26:01.851 --> 26:02.811
What was that?

26:03.770 --> 26:06.064
- We're being filmed!
- Dude, run!

26:07.023 --> 26:08.108
Damn it!

26:14.072 --> 26:14.990
I got it on camera.

26:33.133 --> 26:34.551
- It hurts, asshat.
- Ass…

26:36.970 --> 26:37.846
Do it yourself.

26:37.929 --> 26:39.222
No, do it for me.

26:39.306 --> 26:41.141
- Forget it. You do it.
- I'm sorry. Help me out.

26:44.894 --> 26:46.604
- Turn your head.
- Like this?

26:53.778 --> 26:56.114
You really got hit all over.

26:56.197 --> 26:57.657
You should see the other guys.

26:59.284 --> 27:01.453
- Now, turn the other way.
- What?

27:01.536 --> 27:02.787
Do this side a bit more.

27:03.580 --> 27:04.456
Come on.

27:04.539 --> 27:05.623
What?

27:05.707 --> 27:06.750
Turn your head already.

27:08.918 --> 27:09.794
What are you looking…

27:17.302 --> 27:19.095
Why did you guys fight anyway?

27:19.679 --> 27:22.307
They're not nice guys.

27:22.390 --> 27:23.933
It was just a spat.

27:24.017 --> 27:25.060
I see.

27:25.769 --> 27:27.979
Why didn't you help me from the start?

27:28.063 --> 27:29.814
Why wait until the last minute?

27:29.898 --> 27:32.609
I thought you were good at fighting.

27:33.276 --> 27:35.320
I'm not a good fighter.

27:35.403 --> 27:36.696
Then, you should've run away.

27:39.282 --> 27:41.201
I don't think I'd be good at that either.

27:42.452 --> 27:43.703
Oh, I know.

27:43.787 --> 27:45.663
It's because
you don't like to sweat, right?

27:47.624 --> 27:49.584
Isn't sweating better than bleeding?

27:50.251 --> 27:51.586
You're right. It is better.

27:51.669 --> 27:54.381
Tell me if they bother you again.
I've got the recording.

28:01.471 --> 28:03.390
- What?
- What are you looking at?

28:37.424 --> 28:44.431
UNDERSEA GLASS STUDIO

29:10.540 --> 29:12.417
Do you miss her a lot?

29:13.209 --> 29:14.502
Today? Yeah.

29:15.420 --> 29:16.421
I guess.

29:19.924 --> 29:21.968
You miss your mom a lot too, don't you?

29:25.388 --> 29:26.598
Yeah.

29:28.475 --> 29:29.309
I think…

29:30.852 --> 29:32.645
I miss her even more than I did back then.

29:35.356 --> 29:38.526
Back then, it was all just sad and hard,

29:39.986 --> 29:42.489
and I didn't know what to do.

29:42.989 --> 29:44.407
But now that it's been a while…

29:46.576 --> 29:48.077
I don't know about anything else…

29:51.706 --> 29:52.874
other than the fact that I miss her.

30:04.385 --> 30:05.386
That's why

30:06.930 --> 30:08.223
I hope…

30:09.974 --> 30:12.268
you won't have such a hard time anymore.

30:13.436 --> 30:14.395
Honestly,

30:15.271 --> 30:18.233
I want you to start taking photos again,

30:19.776 --> 30:20.944
meet your friends,

30:21.653 --> 30:23.905
and go out and have fun once in a while.

30:25.281 --> 30:26.783
I want that for you.

30:27.867 --> 30:29.118
Thinking about your mom

30:30.328 --> 30:32.080
and missing her…

30:34.290 --> 30:36.125
isn't hard.

30:39.420 --> 30:42.423
I think it's nice
that I get to think about her.

30:44.926 --> 30:46.094
It is nice, but…

30:48.054 --> 30:49.013
What I'm saying is,

30:50.306 --> 30:52.267
I want you to spend more time having fun

30:52.350 --> 30:55.270
than thinking about Mom.

30:59.023 --> 31:00.108
All right, I hear you.

31:02.360 --> 31:04.737
You're nagging more and more now.

31:19.294 --> 31:20.545
I'll eat it if you won't.

31:23.631 --> 31:25.592
Why do you keep following me around?

31:25.675 --> 31:28.553
I'm letting you hang out with me.
You have no friends.

31:36.436 --> 31:37.979
By the way,
are you really dating Seo-yoon?

31:41.524 --> 31:42.984
Why do you act like total strangers?

31:44.402 --> 31:46.362
We just decided to do that at school.

31:46.446 --> 31:48.114
Why do you even care?

31:48.197 --> 31:49.240
What's that about?

31:51.200 --> 31:52.452
I don't know either.

31:53.202 --> 31:54.203
What's up with that?

31:55.914 --> 31:56.831
What's with them?

31:59.459 --> 32:00.293
No way.

32:02.962 --> 32:04.547
- Is this your first…
- What?

32:08.509 --> 32:10.929
Here we go again.
Why do you always bring up dumb stuff?

32:11.971 --> 32:12.889
Dude.

32:13.431 --> 32:15.683
- It's your first time dating a girl, huh?
- Can we not talk about this?

32:15.767 --> 32:17.727
- What's wrong with you?
- Listen, kiddo.

32:18.519 --> 32:20.021
Here's the thing about dating.

32:20.605 --> 32:23.608
If you don't do what the girl says,
you're in trouble.

32:23.691 --> 32:26.110
But if you only do what she says,

32:26.194 --> 32:27.528
you'll be in bigger trouble.

32:29.572 --> 32:30.573
What does that even mean?

32:31.783 --> 32:32.825
What are you doing?

32:34.702 --> 32:35.578
Jeez, that hurts.

32:35.662 --> 32:36.704
Love hurts.

32:37.538 --> 32:38.790
See?

32:38.873 --> 32:40.083
It's all about timing.

32:42.752 --> 32:45.296
How will you kiss
or make out with her at this rate?

32:45.380 --> 32:46.839
What's the matter with you?

32:46.923 --> 32:48.424
Give it a rest!

32:48.508 --> 32:50.051
Hey, cut it out!

32:51.719 --> 32:53.513
- What are they doing?
- Fine, I'll stop.

32:54.347 --> 32:56.224
- Oh my gosh.
- Kiss!

33:12.657 --> 33:14.283
THE FINALS ARE IN TWO WEEKS, YOU KNOW…

33:29.215 --> 33:30.967
I'M JUST CLEARING MY HEAD FOR A MINUTE!!

33:31.050 --> 33:32.593
WE'VE BEEN HERE FOR TEN MINUTES

33:43.021 --> 33:44.856
YOU'RE A T, AREN'T YOU?

33:44.939 --> 33:46.816
WHAT DOES THAT HAVE TO DO WITH…

33:51.821 --> 33:53.698
You should really study.

33:53.781 --> 33:55.658
I'm just about to start.

33:55.742 --> 33:57.910
Your scribbling says otherwise.

33:57.994 --> 33:58.911
Get started already.

33:58.995 --> 34:00.496
I said I'm going to.

34:17.638 --> 34:20.475
Do you want to go on a date this weekend?

34:28.357 --> 34:29.484
The maximum value is

34:30.359 --> 34:32.028
x equals x squared…

34:33.112 --> 34:35.573
OKAY

35:00.765 --> 35:01.641
Kim Jae-won.

35:02.850 --> 35:03.726
Hey.

35:06.771 --> 35:08.189
- Hi.
- Hi.

35:11.984 --> 35:14.695
I've only ever seen you in your uniform,

35:14.779 --> 35:15.822
so seeing you like this

35:16.697 --> 35:17.740
feels so awkward.

35:19.909 --> 35:22.078
I found a really nice spot earlier.

35:22.161 --> 35:23.329
Do you want to check it out?

35:25.164 --> 35:26.666
- Yeah.
- Let's go.

35:30.795 --> 35:32.296
- Did you have breakfast?
- Yeah.

35:33.548 --> 35:34.841
- What about you?
- Me too.

35:53.192 --> 35:54.026
Ta-da!

35:55.153 --> 35:56.571
Oh my, what's this?

35:56.654 --> 35:58.239
Did you make it yourself?

35:58.322 --> 35:59.323
Yeah.

35:59.407 --> 36:01.617
You're amazing.

36:01.701 --> 36:04.036
It's not that big of a deal.

36:04.120 --> 36:06.038
I'm just used to doing
the housework myself,

36:06.747 --> 36:08.499
so I got good at doing stuff like this.

36:08.583 --> 36:10.209
Oh, did your mom teach you?

36:13.421 --> 36:15.089
It's just me and my dad.

36:15.673 --> 36:16.591
My mom

36:17.466 --> 36:18.759
passed away five years ago.

36:19.594 --> 36:20.469
I see.

36:24.515 --> 36:25.391
I'm sorry.

36:26.475 --> 36:29.770
For some reason,
I feel like I can tell you anything.

36:31.355 --> 36:32.773
Can I try this?

36:32.857 --> 36:34.901
Of course, I made it for you. Hang on.

36:36.611 --> 36:37.653
This one looks good.

36:45.161 --> 36:46.120
How is it?

36:47.455 --> 36:49.874
- Is it good?
- Yeah! It's so good!

36:51.626 --> 36:53.085
- I'm glad.
- It's delicious!

36:55.963 --> 36:57.131
It's so beautiful.

37:14.607 --> 37:15.775
This is nice.

37:56.315 --> 37:57.608
It's interesting.

37:59.819 --> 38:00.653
What is?

38:02.321 --> 38:03.239
It's just…

38:05.616 --> 38:07.868
We haven't known each other long,

38:09.287 --> 38:10.288
but it feels like

38:12.039 --> 38:15.376
we've slowly been building up
all this time together.

38:54.081 --> 38:55.374
Who are you?

38:55.458 --> 38:56.375
What?

38:56.459 --> 38:58.044
No, I mean…

39:01.339 --> 39:02.465
What's wrong?

39:05.176 --> 39:06.177
What's going on?

39:07.845 --> 39:10.139
Wait! Where are you going?

39:10.848 --> 39:11.849
Wait!

39:12.558 --> 39:13.809
Hold on.

39:15.311 --> 39:16.228
Where are you going?

39:20.649 --> 39:22.526
What's wrong?

39:23.944 --> 39:25.321
Where am I?

39:28.783 --> 39:29.700
Here?

39:31.494 --> 39:34.121
We had our date today, remember?

39:36.874 --> 39:39.085
It's me, Jae-won.

39:39.710 --> 39:40.711
Kim Jae-won.

39:43.255 --> 39:44.423
I don't know.

39:47.093 --> 39:48.803
I don't remember anything.

39:49.637 --> 39:52.681
What do you mean you don't remember?

39:53.557 --> 39:54.475
Seo-yoon.

40:42.815 --> 40:43.941
BESTIE

40:53.075 --> 40:55.035
Are you heading home already?

40:55.744 --> 40:57.830
I guess the date
wasn't as good as you thought, huh?

41:00.082 --> 41:01.083
Ji-min.

41:01.792 --> 41:03.878
What's wrong? Did something happen?

41:04.503 --> 41:07.006
I opened my eyes,

41:08.299 --> 41:09.216
and I was on a bus.

41:10.301 --> 41:11.469
But…

41:28.986 --> 41:31.989
CHOI JI-MIN

41:39.246 --> 41:40.664
NOTES ON MY BOYFRIEND KIM JAE-WON

41:46.086 --> 41:47.755
THURSDAY, MAY 22, 2025
NOTHING UNUSUAL

41:47.838 --> 41:49.465
FRIDAY, MAY 23, 2025
ORGANIZED NOTES & JOURNAL, NOTHING UNUSUAL

41:49.548 --> 41:51.175
SATURDAY, MAY 24, 2025: GOT TO SCHOOL LATE
SUNDAY, MAY 25, 2025: STAYED HOME ALL DAY

41:51.258 --> 41:52.801
MONDAY, MAY 26, 2025: HAD A BAD HEADACHE
TUESDAY, MAY 27, 2025: HOSPITAL CHECKUP

41:52.885 --> 41:55.137
FRIDAY, MAY 30, 2025: NOTHING UNUSUAL
SATURDAY, MAY 31, 2025: WILL I GET BETTER?

41:55.221 --> 41:58.682
MONDAY, JUNE 2, 2025
A TALL BOY WHO LOOKED HIGH-STRUNG…

41:58.766 --> 42:01.060
Monday, June 2, 2025.

42:02.436 --> 42:04.772
A tall boy who looked high-strung

42:05.731 --> 42:07.107
walked up to me out of nowhere.

42:09.527 --> 42:11.028
- "Will you go out with me?"
- Will you go out with me?

42:11.612 --> 42:13.447
Junior, Class 2, Kim Jae-won.

42:14.615 --> 42:16.116
I agreed to go out with him.

42:18.661 --> 42:20.704
Maybe I'll get to try something new.

42:22.540 --> 42:24.959
I gave him three conditions.

42:25.459 --> 42:27.127
Rule number one of dating

42:27.211 --> 42:29.213
is to keep communication short.

42:29.296 --> 42:32.383
It'd be a problem if he brought up things
from the day before.

42:33.884 --> 42:34.718
Rule number two

42:35.302 --> 42:37.471
is that we don't talk to each other
until after school.

42:38.722 --> 42:42.268
I need time to sort out
all the information about me and him.

42:44.520 --> 42:46.105
And lastly, rule number three…

42:49.358 --> 42:51.318
is that we don't catch real feelings.

42:52.570 --> 42:54.613
We'll have to break up soon anyway.

42:59.827 --> 43:02.580
So, there's no point
in having deep feelings.

44:03.515 --> 44:05.184
Hey, so…

44:08.979 --> 44:09.938
I'm--

44:10.022 --> 44:11.148
Kim Jae-won.

44:12.441 --> 44:13.317
Right?

44:16.070 --> 44:18.030
Yeah, that's right.

44:24.411 --> 44:25.371
Aren't you cold?

44:28.916 --> 44:29.792
No.

44:35.422 --> 44:36.256
You see…

44:38.634 --> 44:41.512
I seem to have memory issues.

44:41.595 --> 44:43.639
No, I mean…

44:46.475 --> 44:49.478
I have a memory disorder.

44:50.896 --> 44:51.772
It's…

44:52.940 --> 44:56.568
It's called anterograde amnesia.

44:58.445 --> 45:00.030
When I fall asleep,

45:00.114 --> 45:01.573
I forget everything…

45:03.450 --> 45:04.618
that happened that day.

45:07.371 --> 45:09.081
So…

45:10.457 --> 45:11.667
I…

45:12.876 --> 45:13.877
If it's too hard…

45:15.921 --> 45:17.881
you don't have to tell me now.

45:26.098 --> 45:27.057
I'm sorry.

45:28.183 --> 45:30.227
I used you for selfish reasons.

45:32.271 --> 45:33.355
I thought…

45:35.107 --> 45:37.860
maybe I could try something new
even though I'm like this.

45:43.073 --> 45:44.074
You can use me.

45:46.785 --> 45:47.661
What?

45:49.163 --> 45:50.038
So…

45:51.915 --> 45:53.834
if you don't write down
what happened today,

45:55.252 --> 45:57.004
you won't know about it tomorrow, right?

45:58.630 --> 45:59.548
Then,

46:01.008 --> 46:04.219
don't write that you told me
you have a memory disorder.

46:05.012 --> 46:06.805
What do you mean?

46:17.983 --> 46:19.860
I have fun hanging out with you.

46:21.403 --> 46:22.279
And…

46:25.782 --> 46:28.035
I don't want things to change between us.

46:30.204 --> 46:31.121
So,

46:32.331 --> 46:34.249
let's both…

46:36.710 --> 46:38.253
trick tomorrow-you together.

46:45.385 --> 46:48.514
Of course, only if you're okay with it.

46:51.350 --> 46:52.351
Well…

47:02.194 --> 47:03.946
ANTEROGRADE AMNESIA

47:07.324 --> 47:12.037
ANTEROGRADE AMNESIA IS WHEN YOU CAN'T FORM
NEW MEMORIES DUE TO HIPPOCAMPUS DAMAGE

47:25.634 --> 47:26.718
Hi, Kim Jae-won.

47:34.184 --> 47:35.519
Did something good happen?

47:35.602 --> 47:36.478
Yeah.

47:36.562 --> 47:37.437
What is it?

47:39.856 --> 47:41.525
It's a secret. Let's go.

47:41.608 --> 47:42.568
What?

47:44.486 --> 47:45.445
What was that?

47:46.113 --> 47:48.073
Your face is so transparent.

47:49.032 --> 47:49.866
No, it's not.

47:49.950 --> 47:51.535
See? I can read you right now.

47:51.618 --> 47:52.452
Unbelievable.

47:52.536 --> 47:54.079
- See?
- Me?

47:54.997 --> 47:56.498
So, what did you want to tell me?

47:59.501 --> 48:01.628
I wanted to thank you
for calling me yesterday.

48:02.212 --> 48:03.672
You don't have to thank me.

48:04.881 --> 48:07.676
I only do what I want to do
and what I can do.

48:10.304 --> 48:11.305
Right.

48:11.388 --> 48:13.807
It's really dangerous
if people spread rumors

48:14.474 --> 48:15.809
that she has a memory disorder…

48:17.644 --> 48:21.064
because whatever happens,
Seo-yoon won't remember anything.

48:21.690 --> 48:22.524
You're right.

48:24.067 --> 48:26.236
Not everyone in this world is good.

48:28.280 --> 48:29.531
Speaking of which…

48:32.784 --> 48:33.952
are you a good person?

48:40.959 --> 48:41.960
I just…

48:43.378 --> 48:45.797
want to make sure
every new day is a good day for her.

48:46.673 --> 48:47.841
I want her journal

48:48.342 --> 48:50.636
to be filled with happy memories.

48:53.513 --> 48:56.725
Oh, and I asked her not to write
about what happened yesterday.

48:58.310 --> 49:01.146
- What?
- I didn't want her to feel bad

49:01.229 --> 49:03.982
or avoid me because of it.

49:07.110 --> 49:08.987
I figured I should tell you.

49:10.489 --> 49:11.907
Why?

49:14.159 --> 49:15.118
Because…

49:17.037 --> 49:17.954
I'm scared too.

49:18.705 --> 49:19.873
What are you saying?

49:22.417 --> 49:23.251
Anyway,

49:24.294 --> 49:26.672
I think I can trust you now.

49:27.714 --> 49:28.548
Really?

49:29.132 --> 49:31.468
Just don't be irresponsible
and bail on her later.

49:32.052 --> 49:32.928
If that ever happens,

49:33.762 --> 49:35.472
I'll leave the rest to you.

49:35.555 --> 49:37.140
That's exactly what irresponsible is.

49:41.520 --> 49:42.604
Oh, right. I have a girlfriend.

49:46.983 --> 49:48.694
You have a what?

49:48.777 --> 49:50.028
A girlfriend.

49:52.322 --> 49:53.156
A girl…

49:53.240 --> 49:54.908
Look at you, all grown up.

49:54.991 --> 49:56.910
Jeez, what are you doing?

49:56.993 --> 49:58.203
I'm holding a knife here.

49:59.329 --> 50:00.247
I'm jealous.

50:01.790 --> 50:04.042
What are you talking about?

50:04.126 --> 50:05.335
You know what?

50:05.419 --> 50:06.461
That's it.

50:07.546 --> 50:09.840
I need to give you some allowance.

50:10.382 --> 50:13.093
Forget it. You don't have any money.

50:13.176 --> 50:14.428
I have plenty, okay?

50:14.511 --> 50:16.304
Things are going great
at the studio these days.

50:16.388 --> 50:17.681
Look at this.

50:18.765 --> 50:19.766
Here.

50:22.936 --> 50:23.812
Show me a picture.

50:31.027 --> 50:31.903
Is she pretty?

50:41.663 --> 50:45.250
I think I asked to see Seo-yoon alone.
How did this happen?

50:46.209 --> 50:47.127
Anyone?

50:48.920 --> 50:51.131
Well?

50:52.340 --> 50:53.925
Well, finally!

50:54.426 --> 50:56.011
We're done with exams,
so what should we do?

50:57.429 --> 50:58.680
What can we do?

50:59.347 --> 51:02.184
What can we do that's so fun
it will make others jealous?

51:02.267 --> 51:03.310
Do you have to be involved?

51:03.894 --> 51:05.437
Come on, why would you say that?

51:06.021 --> 51:09.524
Is there anything you wanted to do
or any place you wanted to go?

51:10.442 --> 51:13.111
Something I wanted to do…

51:14.029 --> 51:15.572
- Hold on.
- Okay.

51:16.531 --> 51:17.616
Yeah.

51:18.575 --> 51:22.037
We haven't hung out as a group in a while,
and exams are over…

51:22.120 --> 51:24.831
It's nice, isn't it?

51:24.915 --> 51:27.083
Hey, what are you…

51:27.751 --> 51:30.086
Don't touch her. Why would you touch her?

51:30.170 --> 51:32.047
- No, not me.
- What's wrong with you?

51:32.130 --> 51:33.173
It's so cute.

51:34.174 --> 51:35.842
- I know.
- Yeah?

51:35.926 --> 51:37.219
There's a place I want to go.

51:37.302 --> 51:38.178
Where?

51:39.721 --> 51:40.806
I want to go see penguins.

51:42.140 --> 51:43.308
What?

51:43.391 --> 51:45.310
Penguins?

51:53.527 --> 51:54.528
You're good.

52:01.701 --> 52:03.829
- Hey, it's dangerous! Look ahead!
- Jeez, you scared me.

52:04.412 --> 52:06.206
Are you worried about me?

52:09.918 --> 52:11.461
Stop bickering, you two.

52:11.545 --> 52:13.672
Hey, Choi Ji-min. Wait up!

52:14.172 --> 52:15.465
Slow down!

52:29.020 --> 52:30.105
How cute!

52:30.188 --> 52:32.816
- They're super cute.
- They're really cute.

52:33.608 --> 52:34.693
They're so cute!

52:34.776 --> 52:35.735
Ji-min!

52:59.217 --> 53:00.302
What the heck?

53:01.845 --> 53:03.013
Yours too.

53:03.096 --> 53:04.598
Look at your teeth.

53:04.681 --> 53:06.224
Why did you want to see penguins?

53:07.350 --> 53:09.144
Because it's so cute how they toddle.

53:10.061 --> 53:11.521
Don't penguins waddle?

53:11.605 --> 53:13.106
"Toddle" sounds cuter.

53:15.108 --> 53:16.401
I hope we get to see them.

53:16.484 --> 53:18.320
- Penguins…
- Oh, this must be it.

53:18.403 --> 53:20.322
- Oh, here it is.
- Penguins?

53:22.073 --> 53:22.949
What?

53:24.367 --> 53:25.285
Where are the penguins?

53:26.578 --> 53:27.913
THE PENGUINS ARE RESTING TODAY
SEE YOU NEXT TIME

53:27.996 --> 53:28.955
No penguins?

53:29.831 --> 53:32.167
Oh, they're resting.
Did they work too hard yesterday?

53:32.959 --> 53:33.835
It's okay.

53:34.586 --> 53:36.379
Maybe they'll come out if we wait.

53:36.880 --> 53:37.756
Should we check out that side?

53:37.839 --> 53:39.507
- Okay.
- Okay.

53:40.508 --> 53:41.426
It's okay.

53:48.892 --> 53:50.518
This place is amazing.

53:51.686 --> 53:52.979
It's so beautiful.

53:54.022 --> 53:55.148
I thought you might like it.

54:00.820 --> 54:03.406
I had so much fun today.

54:06.493 --> 54:07.494
It's so beautiful.

54:17.879 --> 54:20.090
Kim Jae-won! Come on!

54:21.257 --> 54:22.300
It feels so cool.

54:23.259 --> 54:24.260
Be careful.

54:32.894 --> 54:34.729
No, don't do it.

54:34.813 --> 54:36.856
Seriously, don't do it.
I'll splash you back.

55:17.897 --> 55:20.358
How do you tie your shoelaces like that?

55:38.626 --> 55:39.669
You need to do it this way,

55:40.587 --> 55:41.713
or they'll come undone.

55:43.256 --> 55:44.257
It looks tricky.

55:52.474 --> 55:53.808
It's okay.

55:53.892 --> 55:55.643
I'll tie them for you.

56:00.774 --> 56:02.567
This place is really beautiful.

56:03.610 --> 56:04.486
It is.

56:06.488 --> 56:07.405
Let's

56:08.531 --> 56:09.532
come back here sometime.

56:10.200 --> 56:11.785
Okay, let's come back.

56:17.040 --> 56:18.333
And there goes

56:19.334 --> 56:20.668
another day.

56:30.595 --> 56:31.596
I'll make…

56:33.723 --> 56:35.433
tomorrow-you happy too.

56:43.108 --> 56:45.235
That was so cheesy!

56:45.819 --> 56:48.154
You don't like it?

56:48.863 --> 56:51.866
It's not that I don't like it,
but it was just so cheesy.

56:52.367 --> 56:54.494
That was so cheesy!

56:54.994 --> 56:55.954
I want to go home now.

57:03.419 --> 57:07.465
…HE TIED MY SHOELACES

57:24.357 --> 57:26.317
What's going on? Where are we going?

57:26.401 --> 57:28.570
I don't know either.

57:28.653 --> 57:29.487
You don't?

57:45.211 --> 57:46.087
Ta-da!

57:47.338 --> 57:48.840
- Hello.
- What? Kim Jae-won!

57:48.923 --> 57:52.844
Here are the most handsome
and cutest penguins in the world!

57:52.927 --> 57:54.762
- You're crazy.
- No way.

57:54.846 --> 57:57.182
I told you girls love surprises, didn't I?

57:57.265 --> 57:58.183
See? I was right.

57:58.266 --> 57:59.809
- She's just laughing at me.
- No, she's not!

57:59.893 --> 58:03.229
- I told you I didn't want to do it!
- Oh, shut it. She looks happy.

58:03.313 --> 58:04.939
Hey, come on.

58:05.023 --> 58:06.065
I'm leaving.

58:06.149 --> 58:07.066
No, wait!

58:07.150 --> 58:10.236
Wait, Mr. Penguin!
Let me take a picture first.

58:10.820 --> 58:12.071
You're so cute!

58:12.614 --> 58:15.492
- Take a picture of me too, Ji-min.
- Don't be shy. You look adorable.

58:15.575 --> 58:18.495
Is this why you've been bothering me
the past few days?

58:18.578 --> 58:19.913
What do you think? Not bad, right?

58:19.996 --> 58:22.874
- Come on. Stop it.
- Come here. Please, just once.

58:22.957 --> 58:25.710
- Strike a cute pose.
- No.

58:25.793 --> 58:26.711
Give me a cute pose.

58:26.794 --> 58:29.214
- She seems happy.
- No, forget it.

58:29.297 --> 58:30.590
- Come on.
- Take a picture of me.

58:31.508 --> 58:33.885
- Here we go!
- Let's pose.

58:33.968 --> 58:36.721
One, two, three!

58:45.480 --> 58:46.481
So cute.

59:04.999 --> 59:06.042
…I WAS SO TOUCHED BY JAE-WON

59:11.965 --> 59:14.842
IF ONLY I COULD REMEMBER THIS DAY…

59:22.433 --> 59:25.520
I'll make tomorrow-you happy too.

59:33.194 --> 59:35.238
UNDERSEA GLASS STUDIO

59:52.005 --> 59:53.131
Focus, will you?

59:53.715 --> 59:55.341
Yes, ma'am. I'll focus now.

59:56.593 --> 59:58.094
I listen to you pretty well, don't I?

01:00:00.388 --> 01:00:01.306
Don't I?

01:00:03.766 --> 01:00:06.227
- Hello, sir.
- Hey.

01:00:08.313 --> 01:00:09.522
You're Seo-yoon, right?

01:00:09.606 --> 01:00:11.107
- Yes. Hello.
- I thought so.

01:00:11.190 --> 01:00:12.650
Here you go.

01:00:12.734 --> 01:00:13.776
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

01:00:14.777 --> 01:00:16.112
You're making good progress.

01:00:16.863 --> 01:00:18.364
Do you need my help?

01:00:18.448 --> 01:00:20.241
We're good, Dad. Thanks for the drinks.
You should go rest.

01:00:21.075 --> 01:00:22.785
Okay.

01:00:43.222 --> 01:00:44.390
- What?
- By any chance,

01:00:45.058 --> 01:00:48.978
is your dad Kim Sang-hyeon,
the photographer?

01:00:50.772 --> 01:00:51.606
My dad?

01:00:52.273 --> 01:00:53.316
Yeah.

01:00:53.399 --> 01:00:54.317
Yeah, that's him.

01:00:55.109 --> 01:00:58.696
Are you serious? I'm a huge fan.

01:00:59.280 --> 01:01:00.490
Look.

01:01:01.491 --> 01:01:04.077
- She likes his work.
- I even follow him on Instagram.

01:01:06.287 --> 01:01:08.831
He's one of her favorite photographers.

01:01:08.915 --> 01:01:10.833
Who knew he was your dad?

01:01:10.917 --> 01:01:12.126
That's so cool.

01:01:12.210 --> 01:01:14.212
I want to see. Let me see.

01:01:18.132 --> 01:01:20.134
- Mr. Kim!
- Why are you calling him?

01:01:20.218 --> 01:01:21.636
- Are you busy?
- What are you going to do?

01:01:22.345 --> 01:01:24.806
- Yeah?
- You've got a fan here, sir.

01:01:24.889 --> 01:01:26.724
Hey, what are you doing?

01:01:27.475 --> 01:01:28.393
You're into photography, huh?

01:01:29.102 --> 01:01:29.936
Yes.

01:01:40.154 --> 01:01:41.280
Okay.

01:01:41.364 --> 01:01:43.783
She says she's not just a fan
but a huge fan.

01:01:43.866 --> 01:01:45.576
All right. Thanks.

01:01:47.453 --> 01:01:48.871
Oh, there's more? Okay.

01:01:54.585 --> 01:01:56.921
You're her role model,

01:01:57.004 --> 01:01:59.382
but she's too nervous to say anything.

01:01:59.465 --> 01:02:00.550
You're flattering me.

01:02:03.511 --> 01:02:04.721
Go on.

01:02:08.975 --> 01:02:11.310
She's wondering
why you haven't posted any photos lately.

01:02:13.563 --> 01:02:14.480
I've been busy.

01:02:27.869 --> 01:02:29.662
- I'm home.
- Hey.

01:02:33.458 --> 01:02:35.585
Stop drinking beer. You'll put on weight.

01:02:36.502 --> 01:02:37.462
Did your friends go home?

01:02:38.421 --> 01:02:40.047
Yeah, they did.

01:02:42.759 --> 01:02:43.926
She's pretty.

01:02:47.764 --> 01:02:48.598
Yeah.

01:02:49.599 --> 01:02:50.433
She is.

01:02:50.516 --> 01:02:52.310
My goodness.

01:02:55.188 --> 01:02:57.940
I guess you've been coming home late
because you're busy dating.

01:03:00.985 --> 01:03:01.819
Yeah.

01:03:02.570 --> 01:03:04.238
Still, don't stay out too late.

01:03:04.947 --> 01:03:06.824
It's not good for you to get tired.

01:03:07.825 --> 01:03:08.826
You know, earlier,

01:03:10.077 --> 01:03:13.706
Ji-min said she was a huge fan of yours.

01:03:14.373 --> 01:03:17.001
You saw how she was, right?

01:03:27.178 --> 01:03:30.348
Should we put Mom's things away now?

01:03:34.936 --> 01:03:35.770
Yeah.

01:03:36.562 --> 01:03:38.022
I guess.

01:03:38.648 --> 01:03:39.524
Maybe later.

01:03:43.194 --> 01:03:45.905
Let me fry you an egg or something.

01:03:45.988 --> 01:03:47.323
It's fine. I'll do it.

01:03:47.406 --> 01:03:48.658
- I can do it myself.
- I've got it.

01:03:48.741 --> 01:03:51.452
You always get oil everywhere,
and cleaning that up is more work.

01:03:51.536 --> 01:03:53.788
You little brat,
you think you're better than me.

01:03:53.871 --> 01:03:54.705
How many do you want?

01:04:47.633 --> 01:04:48.759
Hit it properly.

01:04:48.843 --> 01:04:50.678
Go inside. I'll stand here.

01:04:51.721 --> 01:04:54.432
Seo-yoon's parents called me this morning.

01:04:57.018 --> 01:04:58.311
They said Seo-yoon…

01:05:00.354 --> 01:05:02.732
seems to be afraid
of falling asleep these days.

01:05:02.815 --> 01:05:03.983
What? Why?

01:05:05.651 --> 01:05:06.569
I've been

01:05:07.236 --> 01:05:09.822
trying really hard
to make her happy every day.

01:05:10.698 --> 01:05:11.991
That's why.

01:05:13.200 --> 01:05:14.744
The happier and more precious each day is,

01:05:16.329 --> 01:05:18.748
the more it must hurt to forget them.

01:05:33.346 --> 01:05:35.806
JAE-WON DESPERATELY TRIED
NOT TO MAKE EYE CONTACT IN THE CAFETERIA

01:05:35.890 --> 01:05:38.643
Just like the Goryeo Dynasty,

01:05:38.726 --> 01:05:41.395
there's one event that splits
the Joseon Dynasty in half.

01:05:41.479 --> 01:05:44.106
In 1592, after the founding
of the Joseon Dynasty,

01:05:44.190 --> 01:05:45.316
Japan invaded Joseon…

01:05:50.655 --> 01:05:54.200
CHAPTER 6.
HOW THE BRAIN ENCODES MEMORIES

01:06:14.178 --> 01:06:15.096
Thank you!

01:06:15.179 --> 01:06:16.097
I got the banana milk.

01:06:17.556 --> 01:06:18.975
You like this, right?

01:06:39.120 --> 01:06:40.329
UNDERSTANDING PROCEDURAL MEMORY
IN THE MEMORY-PROCESSING SYSTEM

01:06:45.001 --> 01:06:48.379
SUCH AS RIDING A BIKE,
PLAYING AN INSTRUMENT, OR TYPING

01:07:02.226 --> 01:07:04.687
It's summer break soon.

01:07:07.356 --> 01:07:08.190
I know.

01:07:09.316 --> 01:07:10.401
Time flies.

01:07:15.114 --> 01:07:17.324
Oh, I have a gift for you.

01:07:17.408 --> 01:07:19.493
I made it myself. Ta-da.

01:07:19.577 --> 01:07:21.579
Wait. No way.

01:07:22.246 --> 01:07:23.080
What?

01:07:23.622 --> 01:07:25.833
I brought mine to give to you.

01:07:26.459 --> 01:07:28.210
What? No way.

01:07:30.796 --> 01:07:32.006
Look.

01:07:32.089 --> 01:07:35.259
It's really pretty
when you hold it up to the sunlight.

01:07:37.678 --> 01:07:38.596
It's pretty.

01:07:39.138 --> 01:07:39.972
Here.

01:07:41.140 --> 01:07:42.391
- Thanks.
- Thanks.

01:07:42.933 --> 01:07:46.020
You did great for your first try.
It came out better than mine.

01:07:46.729 --> 01:07:49.732
I was a budding artist
until middle school.

01:07:50.274 --> 01:07:52.568
Of course, I've forgotten
pretty much everything now.

01:08:00.117 --> 01:08:00.951
No.

01:08:01.952 --> 01:08:03.370
I'm sure you haven't forgotten.

01:08:07.249 --> 01:08:08.167
It's the kind of thing

01:08:08.918 --> 01:08:12.088
your body remembers, not your mind.

01:08:13.339 --> 01:08:15.216
I saw it on YouTube.

01:08:15.299 --> 01:08:17.176
It's called procedural memory.

01:08:17.259 --> 01:08:19.345
It's not rooted in your brain.

01:08:19.428 --> 01:08:22.765
It's muscle memory rooted in your senses.

01:08:24.558 --> 01:08:26.519
Is procedural memory

01:08:27.144 --> 01:08:28.437
something that never goes away?

01:08:29.230 --> 01:08:31.023
Even if you have amnesia,

01:08:31.107 --> 01:08:33.275
you don't forget how to ride a bike.

01:08:48.582 --> 01:08:49.458
You have a bug on you.

01:08:50.334 --> 01:08:51.460
- Where?
- It's gone.

01:08:51.544 --> 01:08:52.878
- Really?
- Yeah.

01:09:00.594 --> 01:09:02.096
A MIDSUMMER NIGHT FIREWORKS FESTIVAL

01:09:04.598 --> 01:09:05.766
This means you want to go, right?

01:09:06.600 --> 01:09:07.434
All right, let's go.

01:09:08.102 --> 01:09:09.311
- I'll go.
- Look.

01:09:09.395 --> 01:09:10.771
It wasn't meant for you.

01:09:10.855 --> 01:09:12.273
- Then who?
- The 17th?

01:09:14.150 --> 01:09:16.735
You had Korean street food with Jae-won
at a place called Auntie's.

01:09:16.819 --> 01:09:19.363
Try to remember what you ate
as much as possible.

01:09:20.447 --> 01:09:22.199
The answer is on the next page.

01:09:23.784 --> 01:09:25.077
What was it?

01:09:25.578 --> 01:09:26.579
- Hey, Jae-won.
- Hi.

01:09:27.413 --> 01:09:28.247
Hi.

01:09:36.422 --> 01:09:38.090
That scared me! What was that?

01:09:45.681 --> 01:09:47.141
What are you doing?

01:09:54.398 --> 01:09:56.150
- It's pretty cute.
- It is.

01:10:05.409 --> 01:10:06.243
FIREWORKS FESTIVAL

01:10:06.327 --> 01:10:07.828
JAE-WON, JI-MIN, TAE-HUN
MEETING AT THE ENTRANCE AT 7:30 P.M.

01:10:23.719 --> 01:10:26.430
Have fun tomorrow for both of us!

01:10:37.900 --> 01:10:40.653
A MIDSUMMER NIGHT FIREWORKS FESTIVAL

01:10:53.832 --> 01:10:54.792
Hi.

01:10:55.376 --> 01:10:56.210
Hi,

01:10:57.044 --> 01:10:58.003
Kim Jae-won.

01:11:01.840 --> 01:11:03.008
You look pretty.

01:11:09.014 --> 01:11:10.641
- Seo-yoon!
- Kim Jae-won!

01:11:10.724 --> 01:11:12.518
- Ji-min!
- Hey.

01:11:13.686 --> 01:11:14.979
- What took you so long?
- Why are you so late?

01:11:15.062 --> 01:11:16.605
- We're not late.
- You look so pretty today.

01:11:18.399 --> 01:11:20.192
Come and look.

01:11:21.402 --> 01:11:24.154
It's a tarot reading
for "love advice and fortune."

01:11:24.238 --> 01:11:25.489
- What?
- "Love fortune."

01:11:29.159 --> 01:11:30.035
Enjoy.

01:11:30.119 --> 01:11:31.578
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

01:11:32.079 --> 01:11:33.080
- Here.
- Thanks.

01:11:33.789 --> 01:11:35.666
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

01:11:36.917 --> 01:11:37.751
This is so good.

01:11:38.502 --> 01:11:39.545
It looks spicy.

01:11:42.715 --> 01:11:43.590
- You want some?
- Yeah.

01:11:45.426 --> 01:11:46.427
I'll sit on it.

01:11:47.094 --> 01:11:50.264
We still have some time
before the fireworks.

01:11:50.347 --> 01:11:52.933
Do you want to check out that side?
We haven't seen it yet.

01:11:53.017 --> 01:11:55.436
- Over there? Sure.
- All right.

01:11:55.519 --> 01:11:56.895
- Hey.
- What?

01:11:57.479 --> 01:11:58.564
Do you want to get ice cream?

01:11:59.523 --> 01:12:01.525
Ice cream? Sounds good.

01:12:02.151 --> 01:12:03.444
Let's get ice cream.

01:12:07.614 --> 01:12:09.158
Hey, Seo-yoon.

01:12:09.241 --> 01:12:10.367
Yeah?

01:12:11.535 --> 01:12:12.953
Why don't we check out that side?

01:12:13.954 --> 01:12:14.788
Okay.

01:12:14.872 --> 01:12:15.789
Yeah.

01:12:23.839 --> 01:12:26.508
COUNTRY'S LARGEST CRUISE FIREWORKS SHOW

01:12:27.593 --> 01:12:29.470
Please watch your step. It's slippery.

01:14:01.228 --> 01:14:02.521
I don't want to forget this.

01:14:10.696 --> 01:14:11.780
You won't forget.

01:14:25.836 --> 01:14:27.004
No memory…

01:14:28.547 --> 01:14:30.591
ever completely disappears.

01:14:33.385 --> 01:14:34.553
That's what I believe.

01:14:43.395 --> 01:14:44.271
I…

01:14:48.192 --> 01:14:50.152
I think I broke the third rule.

01:14:52.446 --> 01:14:53.322
I broke it…

01:14:56.033 --> 01:14:57.201
a long time ago.

01:15:42.621 --> 01:15:45.332
HAN SEO-YOON

01:15:45.415 --> 01:15:47.543
CHECK IMPORTANT NOTES
IN THE "JOURNAL" FOLDER

01:15:47.626 --> 01:15:53.173
ALARM

01:16:11.316 --> 01:16:14.278
YOU HAVE MEMORY DISORDER FROM AN ACCIDENT
CHECK YOUR COMPUTER ON THE DESK!

01:16:14.361 --> 01:16:16.822
ALWAYS KEEP THE NOTEBOOK IN YOUR BAG

01:16:16.905 --> 01:16:19.366
BE CAREFUL AT SCHOOL!
ONLY YOUR FRIEND JI-MIN KNOWS!

01:16:41.847 --> 01:16:43.307
- Is this for real?
- I'm blocking you right away.

01:16:43.390 --> 01:16:44.808
Stop lying, man.

01:16:45.392 --> 01:16:47.603
I'm blocking your move.

01:16:47.686 --> 01:16:49.438
Gi-hun. Throw it here!

01:16:49.521 --> 01:16:51.982
- Go, go!
- Hand it over!

01:16:52.065 --> 01:16:54.109
It seems right to split it like this,
but you shouldn't.

01:16:54.192 --> 01:16:55.944
The word "gatda"

01:16:56.028 --> 01:16:58.155
is a compound of "ga,"
meaning "to go," and…

01:17:00.490 --> 01:17:02.242
Not long until senior year now.

01:17:02.326 --> 01:17:03.660
I know.

01:17:03.744 --> 01:17:06.246
I guess we won't be able to
have fun anymore.

01:17:06.330 --> 01:17:07.205
Probably not.

01:17:08.457 --> 01:17:10.292
I'd love to go on another outing.

01:17:10.375 --> 01:17:13.128
Remember when the three of us went to
the aquarium and fireworks festival?

01:17:14.296 --> 01:17:15.589
Yeah, we did.

01:17:18.842 --> 01:17:20.594
I'm getting a bit hungry.

01:17:20.677 --> 01:17:22.679
Do you want some tteokbokki
on the way home?

01:17:23.305 --> 01:17:24.598
Yeah, sounds good.

01:17:24.681 --> 01:17:26.350
- I'm down.
- Let's go.

01:17:29.353 --> 01:17:30.771
Should we go to Auntie's?

01:17:30.854 --> 01:17:31.730
Sure.

01:17:31.813 --> 01:17:34.107
I'm excited. The food there is so good.

01:17:34.191 --> 01:17:35.067
I know, right?

01:17:43.200 --> 01:17:50.207
All I can offer you now is

01:17:50.290 --> 01:17:56.213
Good night, good dream, goodbye

01:17:58.006 --> 01:18:00.926
Good night, good dream…

01:18:04.763 --> 01:18:06.848
Senior year came in the blink of an eye.

01:18:08.767 --> 01:18:11.728
Well, everything does for me, but still.

01:18:11.812 --> 01:18:13.522
That's the third time you've said that.

01:18:14.731 --> 01:18:15.691
Is it?

01:18:17.901 --> 01:18:18.985
When you go to college,

01:18:19.653 --> 01:18:21.822
I'll still be a high school student.

01:18:21.905 --> 01:18:24.533
Who will I hang out with then?

01:18:24.616 --> 01:18:25.909
You can go to college too.

01:18:26.660 --> 01:18:27.953
Why not apply to art school?

01:18:28.537 --> 01:18:29.371
Art school?

01:18:31.540 --> 01:18:33.458
Do you really think I can go to college?

01:18:33.542 --> 01:18:34.876
Of course.

01:18:35.460 --> 01:18:36.336
Actually,

01:18:37.295 --> 01:18:38.880
I've been drawing a lot lately.

01:18:41.341 --> 01:18:42.426
Let's see it.

01:18:42.509 --> 01:18:43.385
Hold on.

01:18:50.976 --> 01:18:51.810
By any chance…

01:18:54.146 --> 01:18:56.440
do you know who this is?

01:18:58.525 --> 01:19:00.527
Take a look. Do you recognize him?

01:19:04.823 --> 01:19:06.199
It's strange.

01:19:06.283 --> 01:19:07.743
I keep drawing him for some reason.

01:19:12.414 --> 01:19:13.415
Do you not recognize him?

01:19:19.004 --> 01:19:20.172
Who could it be?

01:19:22.382 --> 01:19:24.676
I know this might sound funny…

01:19:26.636 --> 01:19:27.512
but…

01:19:29.347 --> 01:19:30.932
he somehow feels familiar.

01:19:37.022 --> 01:19:38.190
Whatever.

01:19:41.026 --> 01:19:43.904
I have a favor to ask you.

01:19:45.781 --> 01:19:46.656
You see,

01:19:47.949 --> 01:19:50.535
I was born with a weak heart.

01:19:51.161 --> 01:19:54.748
So, I've been getting
regular checkups and everything.

01:19:55.499 --> 01:19:57.125
But recently,

01:19:57.209 --> 01:20:00.253
it suddenly got a lot worse.

01:20:02.506 --> 01:20:03.381
So…

01:20:07.219 --> 01:20:08.261
I thought…

01:20:09.513 --> 01:20:10.472
Just in case…

01:20:12.808 --> 01:20:14.351
I thought I should ask you ahead of time.

01:20:14.434 --> 01:20:16.228
If you're about to say
something ridiculous, don't.

01:20:19.022 --> 01:20:19.981
I promised…

01:20:22.567 --> 01:20:25.237
to make Seo-yoon happy

01:20:25.320 --> 01:20:26.571
day after day.

01:20:30.826 --> 01:20:32.702
But I don't know
how much time I have left.

01:20:34.079 --> 01:20:35.497
I could collapse at any moment.

01:20:38.542 --> 01:20:39.918
You're going to be fine.

01:20:43.171 --> 01:20:44.548
Nothing's going to happen.

01:21:17.163 --> 01:21:20.208
KIM JAE-WON

01:21:22.544 --> 01:21:24.546
The person you're trying to reach
is unavailable.

01:21:24.629 --> 01:21:26.172
You'll be charged after the beep.

01:21:41.563 --> 01:21:43.231
BESTIE

01:21:45.567 --> 01:21:46.651
Hello?

01:21:47.235 --> 01:21:48.236
Hi, Ji-min.

01:22:34.616 --> 01:22:35.575
Thank you.

01:22:38.453 --> 01:22:39.829
Thank you, Ji-min.

01:22:42.123 --> 01:22:43.249
My goodness.

01:22:46.711 --> 01:22:48.964
Thank you for coming.

01:23:17.033 --> 01:23:17.993
Are you okay?

01:23:58.950 --> 01:24:00.201
If I die…

01:24:04.080 --> 01:24:05.457
If I die…

01:24:08.084 --> 01:24:09.794
erase me from Seo-yoon's journal.

01:24:38.323 --> 01:24:44.370
CHECK YOUR JOURNAL ON THE COMPUTER
WHEN YOU WAKE UP IN THE MORNING

01:24:47.540 --> 01:24:49.667
JOURNAL (ALL)

01:24:49.751 --> 01:24:51.878
KEY ENTRIES (JUNE)

01:24:51.961 --> 01:24:54.089
MONDAY, JUNE 2, 2025

01:24:54.172 --> 01:24:55.757
JUNIOR, CLASS 2, KIM JAE-WON

01:24:57.258 --> 01:25:01.221
JOURNAL

01:25:21.116 --> 01:25:23.201
- No, I--
- All right, then.

01:25:35.797 --> 01:25:36.965
I WENT TO KARAOKE WITH JAE-WON

01:25:37.048 --> 01:25:38.216
JAE-WON WAITED FOR ME BY THE GATE

01:25:38.299 --> 01:25:39.134
I TOLD JAE-WON I WANTED TO SEE PENGUINS

01:25:40.343 --> 01:25:41.511
Look, Jae-won!

01:26:02.782 --> 01:26:03.700
ABOUT KIM JAE-WON!

01:26:03.783 --> 01:26:04.993
KIM JAE-WON!!

01:26:05.076 --> 01:26:06.828
YOU HAVE MEMORY DISORDER FROM AN ACCIDENT
CHECK YOUR COMPUTER ON THE DESK!

01:26:06.911 --> 01:26:11.791
KIM JAE-WON

01:27:20.485 --> 01:27:23.363
KIM JAE-WON

01:27:31.621 --> 01:27:32.747
I WAS WAITING FOR IT TO SNOW,

01:27:32.830 --> 01:27:34.415
TURNING THE WORLD PURE WHITE,
LIKE A BLANK CANVAS

01:27:46.261 --> 01:27:49.055
SATURDAY, DECEMBER 27, 2025

01:28:18.084 --> 01:28:19.419
- Listen, honey.
- Yeah?

01:28:19.502 --> 01:28:21.587
Is there anything you want to ask us?

01:28:22.213 --> 01:28:24.799
You've been having trouble
sleeping lately.

01:28:26.801 --> 01:28:29.429
No, I fell asleep
pretty quickly last night.

01:28:29.512 --> 01:28:30.346
That's a relief.

01:28:44.360 --> 01:28:47.113
There's no medical explanation for it
at this point,

01:28:47.196 --> 01:28:49.574
but the fact that your symptoms
are getting better

01:28:49.657 --> 01:28:51.200
is definitely a good sign.

01:28:52.702 --> 01:28:54.120
It's been a hard journey.

01:28:54.620 --> 01:28:55.872
Thank you.

01:28:55.955 --> 01:28:57.498
Whether it's an image

01:28:57.582 --> 01:28:59.959
or a feeling of some kind,

01:29:00.043 --> 01:29:01.919
if anything comes to mind,

01:29:02.003 --> 01:29:04.130
try to dig deep and explore it.

01:29:05.214 --> 01:29:06.049
Okay.

01:29:07.133 --> 01:29:09.093
Have you left the hospital?

01:29:09.635 --> 01:29:10.636
What did your doctor say?

01:29:10.720 --> 01:29:12.805
She said my symptoms are getting better.

01:29:13.848 --> 01:29:14.682
Really?

01:29:15.266 --> 01:29:17.643
Oh, I'm so glad.

01:29:18.895 --> 01:29:22.774
My memory hasn't been resetting
for the past few days,

01:29:23.566 --> 01:29:25.860
but I still don't remember anything
from after the accident.

01:29:29.280 --> 01:29:30.114
I feel like

01:29:30.907 --> 01:29:34.285
I'm still forgetting something important.

01:29:36.537 --> 01:29:37.580
It'll get better, right?

01:29:53.513 --> 01:29:55.765
I still can't remember who he is,

01:29:55.848 --> 01:29:58.434
but I thought maybe I'd remember
if I kept drawing.

01:30:55.825 --> 01:30:56.826
I'm sorry.

01:31:15.428 --> 01:31:22.435
KIM JAE-WON

01:31:24.312 --> 01:31:29.317
CARDIOLOGY

01:31:45.833 --> 01:31:47.710
KIM JAE-WON

01:31:54.133 --> 01:31:59.222
KIM JAE-WON

01:32:12.735 --> 01:32:13.861
Seo-yoon.

01:32:25.748 --> 01:32:28.709
DON'T FORGET KIM JAE-WON

01:32:30.169 --> 01:32:31.003
What…

01:32:32.463 --> 01:32:33.464
is this?

01:32:50.439 --> 01:32:53.818
DON'T FORGET KIM JAE-WON

01:33:12.169 --> 01:33:14.005
KIM JAE-WON!!

01:33:14.088 --> 01:33:17.550
HAESOL HIGH, JUNIOR, CLASS 2, LITTLE CURT,
MBTI UNCLEAR, ALLERGIC TO PEACHES

01:33:17.633 --> 01:33:19.635
ABOUT KIM JAE-WON!
HIS DAD IS PHOTOGRAPHER KIM SANG-HYEON

01:33:41.407 --> 01:33:44.160
I GAVE HIM THREE CONDITIONS

01:33:44.243 --> 01:33:47.496
RULE NUMBER THREE
DON'T CATCH REAL FEELINGS!

01:33:56.172 --> 01:33:57.131
Will you go out with me?

01:33:59.091 --> 01:33:59.967
Okay.

01:34:01.135 --> 01:34:02.553
I'd like that. Let's go out.

01:34:03.054 --> 01:34:05.806
- I'm going to start messing with you.
- Wait a minute.

01:34:05.890 --> 01:34:07.683
Hey! You can't do that.

01:34:08.809 --> 01:34:09.643
What?

01:34:10.353 --> 01:34:11.562
Where are you going?

01:34:12.438 --> 01:34:14.857
All I can offer you now is

01:34:14.940 --> 01:34:17.526
Good dream

01:34:20.988 --> 01:34:22.615
This is Jae-won's secret spot.

01:34:23.866 --> 01:34:25.409
It's just a beach, actually.

01:34:25.493 --> 01:34:26.911
But you said it was your secret spot.

01:34:26.994 --> 01:34:27.828
That's true.

01:34:32.208 --> 01:34:33.751
Oh, be careful.

01:34:36.962 --> 01:34:38.381
You must be hot. Have some water.

01:34:39.632 --> 01:34:40.508
Thanks.

01:34:49.767 --> 01:34:50.810
Hi.

01:34:50.893 --> 01:34:51.727
Hi.

01:34:51.811 --> 01:34:53.396
One, two, three.

01:34:53.479 --> 01:34:54.480
Say cheese!

01:34:55.648 --> 01:34:57.024
It's a video.

01:34:57.108 --> 01:34:59.193
- Oh, come on!
- Jeez.

01:35:17.545 --> 01:35:19.505
UNDERSEA GLASS STUDIO

01:35:21.590 --> 01:35:23.717
FOR RENT

01:35:35.020 --> 01:35:35.980
Hello.

01:35:47.032 --> 01:35:47.867
Well…

01:35:48.742 --> 01:35:51.829
I wasn't sure
if I should give this to you or not.

01:35:54.582 --> 01:35:57.251
But I think you should have it, Seo-yoon.

01:36:00.212 --> 01:36:01.088
Right.

01:36:22.193 --> 01:36:23.235
I think deep down,

01:36:24.737 --> 01:36:25.863
Jae-won…

01:36:26.947 --> 01:36:30.075
wanted to leave
a part of himself with you.

01:36:34.872 --> 01:36:35.789
I'm sorry.

01:36:38.250 --> 01:36:41.337
I don't even remember him.

01:36:43.464 --> 01:36:44.340
Seo-yoon.

01:36:46.884 --> 01:36:48.511
As time goes by,

01:36:49.303 --> 01:36:51.347
everyone's memories start to fade.

01:36:53.641 --> 01:36:56.852
But what remains in your heart…

01:36:58.896 --> 01:37:00.231
never changes.

01:37:39.603 --> 01:37:40.437
Seo-yoon.

01:37:41.021 --> 01:37:41.897
Kim Jae-won!

01:37:43.607 --> 01:37:45.693
But it's a crab, so it moves sideways.

01:37:46.610 --> 01:37:47.820
- Hi!
- Hi.

01:37:47.903 --> 01:37:48.946
Hello.

01:37:50.447 --> 01:37:52.950
Gosh, it's stunning.

01:38:56.889 --> 01:38:58.265
You won't forget.

01:39:00.059 --> 01:39:01.310
No memory…

01:39:04.229 --> 01:39:06.106
ever completely disappears.

01:39:11.695 --> 01:39:12.863
That's what I believe.

01:39:14.406 --> 01:39:16.367
Let's come back here sometime.

01:39:16.867 --> 01:39:18.410
Okay, let's come back.

01:39:39.932 --> 01:39:41.600
Scars don't disappear.

01:39:44.436 --> 01:39:46.355
But the pain doesn't last forever.

01:39:52.611 --> 01:39:53.570
If everyone else

01:39:54.154 --> 01:39:56.448
is forgetting you little by little…

01:40:00.077 --> 01:40:00.994
then I'll…

01:40:02.955 --> 01:40:04.873
try to remember you little by little.

01:40:52.921 --> 01:40:56.008
CHOO YOUNG-WOO

01:40:58.260 --> 01:41:01.430
SHIN SI-A

01:41:04.266 --> 01:41:07.519
DIRECTOR KIM HYE-YOUNG

01:41:19.490 --> 01:41:26.455
EVEN IF THIS LOVE DISAPPEARS TONIGHT

01:45:50.927 --> 01:45:55.932
Subtitle translation by: Hannah Og Nam
